/*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*\
  flowsheetDict --- ED03 the stack is a RECORD, and the velocity is derived
  ===========================================================================

  The SAME NaCl chemistry as ed01 (0.1 mol/kg diluate against a 0.5 mol/kg
  concentrate, Neosepta CMX/AMX), run through a stack that the case NAMES
  instead of typing:

      stack EUR2C-7P18;

  -- the bench unit of Geraldes & Afonso, J. Membr. Sci. 360 (2010)
  499-508, as a `kind edStack` record in data/standards/assets/.  What the
  record supplies, and what the operation therefore no longer declares:

      membranes        CMX_AMX        (the IEM pair)
      cellPairs        7
      activeArea       0.140 m2       THE CELL-PAIR AREA OF THE WHOLE STACK
      channel          0.77 mm x 0.114 m x 0.175 m, mesh spacer, porosity 0.90
      hydraulicPasses  1
      massTransfer     Sh = 0.29 Re^0.5 Sc^0.33   (fitted to THIS stack)
      limits           i_max, T_max

  WHAT A STUDENT SEES HERE.

  (1) THE VELOCITY IS NOT A KNOB.  It used to be typed as
      `linearVelocity 0.05 m/s;` beside a flow the unit already had on its
      inlet stream -- two homes for one fact, and nothing checked them
      against each other, while the velocity sets the mass-transfer
      coefficient and therefore the limiting current.  Here the diluate
      feed carries 175 L/h; the record says seven channels run side by
      side in one hydraulic pass, each 0.114 m wide and 0.77 mm high; and
      the run prints
          u = Q / (n W h) = 175 L/h / (7 x 0.114 x 7.7e-4) = 0.0791 m/s
      which is the paper's own 0.080 m/s for that flow rate.  Change the
      feed and the velocity follows.  Declare a velocity beside `stack`
      and the run REFUSES by name.

  (2) VITOR'S RULE ON THE AREA, printed as arithmetic: `activeArea` is the
      CELL-PAIR area of the whole stack, so this 0.140 m2 stack carries
      0.140 m2 of cation-exchange membrane AND 0.140 m2 of anion-exchange
      membrane (0.280 m2 in total), and the current density is taken on
      the 0.020 m2 one cell pair presents.  Nothing stores any of those
      three derivatives.

  (3) THE ESTIMATES ANNOUNCE THEMSELVES.  Four values in the record are
      not in the paper -- the spacer porosity, the Schmidt exponent (which
      the paper POSTULATES rather than fits), and both limits -- and each
      prints an `[estimate]` line with the note saying how to verify it,
      and reaches the end-of-run caveat block.

  (4) THE LIMITING CURRENT IS PREDICTED, not read off a declared transport
      number: the run prints D_eff, k_c,eff, the limiting transport number
      of every ion at each membrane, both membranes' limiting current, and
      -- because NaCl is a single salt -- the classical Eq. 16 beside the
      general Eq. 15, which agree.

      diluateFeed     ->  +--------------------+ -> diluate
                          | EUR2C-7P18, 7 pairs|
      concentrateFeed ->  |   CMX / AMX        | -> concentrate
                          +--------------------+
                                   | (power, energy wire)
                                   v
                              rectifier (electricLoad)

  A bench stack of seven cell pairs in ONE pass removes a few per cent of
  the diluate's sodium, which is why a real bench run RECIRCULATES the
  diluate through a tank.  That batch arrangement is not modelled here.
\*---------------------------------------------------------------------------*/

// stream state lives on disk in 0/ (per-stream files); flowsheetDict is TOPOLOGY only

units
(
    {
        name        edStack;
        type        electrodialysisStack;
        inputs      ( diluateFeed  concentrateFeed );
        outputs     ( diluate  concentrate );

        operation
        {
            stack             EUR2C-7P18;   // the HARDWARE, as a record
            current           2.0;          // A (raw SI) -- 100 A/m2, below both i_lim and the record's i_max
            xi                0.9;          // current efficiency (declared, not defaulted)
            E_electrodes      1.5;          // V (raw SI) -- lumped electrode overpotential (announced)
        }

        energyOutputs
        (
            { name power;  kind work;  expression "W_electric";  unit W; }
        );
    }
    {
        name        rectifier;
        type        electricLoad;
        operation   { eta 1.0; }
        energyInputs
        (
            { from edStack.power;  kind work;  target W_shaft; }
        );
    }
);
